From: athanor <kernel@athanor.os>
Subject: [PATCH] compiler.h: keep KCFI_REFERENCE() out of modules

KCFI_REFERENCE() takes the address of an asm function in a discarded
section so that the compiler emits its __kcfi_typeid_ symbol, which
SYM_TYPED_FUNC_START() resolves when vmlinux is linked. Its users
(__memset, __memmove, __clear_pages_unrolled, copy_page) sit in
arch/x86 headers that every translation unit includes, modules too.

In a module the reference resolves nothing: the typed function and its
preamble are in vmlinux. It is not harmless either: modpost reads the
undefined symbol from .discard.addressable before the linker drops the
section, so every module counts as a user of the symbol. With
CONFIG_CFI=y and __clear_pages_unrolled exported GPL-only, no non-GPL
module builds on x86_64 any more:

  ERROR: modpost: GPL-incompatible module t.ko uses GPL-only symbol '__clear_pages_unrolled'

for a module whose whole source is #include <linux/mm.h>.

Leave the reference to vmlinux, as is already done for the decompressor
(__DISABLE_EXPORTS) and the vDSO.
---
--- a/include/linux/compiler.h
+++ b/include/linux/compiler.h
@@ -241,10 +241,13 @@
 
 #endif /* __KERNEL__ */
 
-#if defined(CONFIG_CFI) && !defined(__DISABLE_EXPORTS) && !defined(BUILD_VDSO)
+#if defined(CONFIG_CFI) && !defined(__DISABLE_EXPORTS) && !defined(BUILD_VDSO) && !defined(MODULE)
 /*
  * Force a reference to the external symbol so the compiler generates
- * __kcfi_typid.
+ * __kcfi_typid. Only vmlinux consumes it, through SYM_TYPED_FUNC_START(): in
+ * a module the reference resolves nothing and only makes modpost count the
+ * module as a user of the symbol, which rejects a non-GPL module whenever the
+ * symbol is exported GPL-only.
  */
 #define KCFI_REFERENCE(sym) __ADDRESSABLE(sym)
 #else
